<title>POLAND: ZLOTY FIXED WEAKER AT -0.75 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</title>
<headline>ZLOTY FIXED WEAKER AT -0.75 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4940 to the dollar, down from 3.4730 on Monday and at 1.8755 to the mark, down from 1.8710, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.75 percent weaker than the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, against Monday's fix at -0.38 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
